Agents in consuming repos hold board writes back: they ask before a karr write, pass --local-only to avoid the push, read a "do not push" from their brief as covering the board, or stay local for the rest of a session after one failed push. The shared rules publish-gate and board-karr (skills library) now say the board is outside the gate; the two shipped skills have to say the same.

kanban-issues-karr-coordination: a short section that the board is how agents, sessions and machines exchange work, that a card not pushed does not exist for anyone else, that the push is wanted and never asked for; what --local-only is for (a configured remote that cannot be reached) and that karr sync catches up afterwards; what to do when a push fails; card text is as public as the repository.

kanban-issues-karr-ticket: the notes and the handoff push the board and that is intended even when the brief says not to push (that means commits and tags); the "sync" under "What you do not do" means the command, not the automatic sync of edit/handoff.

